83	// Ambient pad that holds for the duration of a yellow-halo combo (≥4) and
84	// thickens further at white-bullet tier (≥8). Voices C2/C3/G3 are common to
85	// both the bassteroid C-major bed and the comet's C-rooted phrygian cluster,
86	// so they layer pleasantly with both. The "third voice" frequency glides
87	// between E4 (major third, bright with bass field) and Eb4 (minor third,
88	// neutral with the comet's b2/tritone dissonance) — controlled by
89	// setHaloAmbientCometMode. On top sits a slow, looping melody voice playing
90	// a "determined" 8-step motif drawn entirely from mode-invariant pitches
91	// (C, D, F, G), so the figure stays musical regardless of the wave's mode
92	// without fighting the comet's b2/tritone cluster.
