2	
3	// Background pulsar + parallax planets. The pulsar spins continuously (twin
4	// magnetic-axis beams sweep around the core), pulses softly on every beat,
5	// and emits a much louder, longer flare on each wave clear, accompanied by
6	// a deep "brrrmmm" drone. Across waves it grows and drifts toward the screen
7	// centre, surrounded by a faint pulsar-wind nebula. The two silhouetted
8	// planets grow much faster than the pulsar (one harder than the other) and
9	// saturate/darken as they fill more of the frame, selling the "camera is
10	// approaching the system" feel. All wave-driven values are read from a
11	// smoothed displayWaveLevel so wave transitions glide rather than snap.
12	
13	type Vec3 = { x: number; y: number; z: number };
14	
15	type Planet = {
